Patch 6504: a title port may point a read-only cellFs open or a stat at another host file, and name the size a stat reports (g_ps3_fs_path_ops, NULL by default).

New header include/ps3emu/fs_path_ops.h: a resolver, resolve(guest_path, host_path, cap, virtual_size). cellFsOpen (read-only: not
O_WRONLY, O_RDWR, O_CREAT or O_TRUNC) and cellFsStat call it right after the guest path was translated to a host path, whether or not the
translated file exists; the port may replace the host path in place, and for cellFsStat set the size to report (regular files). It never
runs for writes or directory listings. With the pointer NULL: one atomic load per read-only open and per stat, nothing else changes.
Use in J-Stars: the mods folder serves files the game opens by a name that is in no archive (voice banks and loading tips of an added
fighter): the resolver answers with the mod's file, or with the archive a window of which is the file; the virtual-file view of patch 6502
then serves the pinned bytes. Upstream candidate (general: "let a port answer a path with its own file"). Only ppu_fs.cpp translates paths in
the J-Stars build, so only it is hooked; sys_fs.c and libs/filesystem/cellFs.c are not.
Test: the J-Stars host test installer/tools/mods_overlay_test.sh (resolver glue, with the toolkit); the patch itself is checked by the
port syntax check (ppu_fs.cpp compiles) and by export_toolkit.py applying it.

diff --git a/include/ps3emu/fs_path_ops.h b/include/ps3emu/fs_path_ops.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/ps3emu/fs_path_ops.h
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+/*
+ * ps3recomp - port path resolver for cellFs (runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp).
+ *
+ * A title port may answer a guest path with a host path of its own, for a file the
+ * game opens read-only by a name that is in no archive and not (or not only) in the
+ * game tree: cellFsOpen and cellFsStat call resolve() right after the guest path has
+ * been translated to a host path. The port may replace that host path (in place) and,
+ * for cellFsStat, the size the guest sees. Use: a port that serves files a mod keeps in
+ * its own folder under the names the game asks for; paired with ps3emu/fs_vfile.h when
+ * the bytes must come from the port's own open file or a window of another file.
+ *
+ * g_ps3_fs_path_ops is NULL by default, and then nothing changes: one atomic load per
+ * read-only cellFsOpen and per cellFsStat.
+ *
+ * Contract:
+ *  - resolve(guest_path, host_path, cap, virtual_size): host_path holds the translated
+ *    host path on entry (a NUL-terminated string in a buffer of cap bytes). Return 0 to
+ *    leave it, or 1 after writing the replacement into host_path (it must fit cap).
+ *    virtual_size is NULL for cellFsOpen; for cellFsStat it points at UINT64_MAX on
+ *    entry, and the port may set the size to report (it is applied to regular files only).
+ *    It must not call back into cellFs. Called for read-only opens (not O_WRONLY, O_RDWR,
+ *    O_CREAT or O_TRUNC) and for stats by path, never for writes or directory listings.
+ *  - May be called from any guest thread.
+ */
+#ifndef PS3EMU_FS_PATH_OPS_H
+#define PS3EMU_FS_PATH_OPS_H
+
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+typedef struct ps3_fs_path_ops {
+    int (*resolve)(const char* guest_path, char* host_path, size_t cap, uint64_t* virtual_size);
+} ps3_fs_path_ops;
+
+/* Defined in runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp. NULL = no resolver. */
+extern const ps3_fs_path_ops* volatile g_ps3_fs_path_ops;
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif /* PS3EMU_FS_PATH_OPS_H */
